---
/**
 * Reverts to light only when the visitor explicitly asked for it.
 *
 * The site is dark by default: `<html class="dark" style="color-scheme: dark">`
 * is written directly in BaseLayout, so the page is already dark before this
 * runs — and stays dark even with JavaScript disabled. This script's only job
 * is to undo that for someone who clicked the toggle.
 *
 * `is:inline` is required: Astro must NOT bundle or defer it, because it has to
 * run synchronously in <head> ahead of any rendering. A hydrated island could
 * not do this — islands hydrate after the first paint by definition.
 *
 * The OS preference is deliberately ignored. Dark is the design default here,
 * not a mirror of the system.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  if (localStorage.getItem('theme') === 'light') {
    document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark');
    document.documentElement.style.colorScheme = 'light';
  }
</script>
